# Enumeration

## Nmap Scan

First, perform a service and version scan.

```bash
nmap -T5 -sV -sC -Pn 10.129.31.17 -v
```

Output:

```text
PORT     STATE SERVICE         VERSION
22/tcp   open  ssh             OpenSSH 8.2p1 Ubuntu 4ubuntu0.5
80/tcp   open  http            nginx 1.18.0 (Ubuntu)
9091/tcp open  xmltec-xmlmail?
```

Interesting findings:

- SSH available on port 22.
- Nginx web server running on port 80.
- Unusual service running on port 9091.
- HTTP redirects to:

```text
http://soccer.htb
```

Add the hostname locally:

```bash
echo "10.129.31.17 soccer.htb" | sudo tee -a /etc/hosts
```

